The '''Jedi Temple training ground''' was a courtyard in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on [[Coruscant]] used for [[Jedi training]], including the teaching of [[youngling]]s. It was the location of an [[Great Tree (Coruscant)|ancient tree]] that was imbued with the powers of [[the Force]]. The tree was removed from the complex after the rise of the [[Galactic Empire]], when the [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]], [[Darth Sidious]], converted the Jedi Temple into the Imperial Palace.

==Description==
The training ground was a courtyard in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on [[Coruscant]].<ref name="The Wrong Jedi" /> It was located near the base of the temple's central spire<ref name="The Wrong Jedi Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-wrong-jedi-trivia-gallery|text="The Wrong Jedi" Trivia Gallery}}</ref> and was used for the training of [[Jedi]], including [[youngling]]s. At its heart was an ancient tree<ref name="The Wrong Jedi" /> that was imbued with the powers of [[the Force]].<ref name="Shattered Empire 4">[[Shattered Empire 4|''Shattered Empire'' 4]]</ref>

==History==
[[File:TempleDuelTrainingGround-TWJ.png|thumb|left|300px|Anakin Skywalker duels Barriss Offee in the training ground]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], the training ground was used for the training of younglings. [[Jedi Master]] [[Tera Sinube]] taught a class of younglings there when a [[Duel at the Jedi Temple|lightsaber duel]] broke out between [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and the rogue [[Padawan]] [[Barriss Offee]], whom Skywalker was attempting to take into custody after learning that she had [[Bombing of the Jedi Temple hangar|bombed]] the Jedi Temple due to her belief that the [[Jedi High Council]] had become corrupt due to their leadership over the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] in the war. Skywalker disarmed the Padawan and used the Force to [[Telekinesis|telekinetically]] slam her into the ancient tree, at which point she was taken into custody.<ref name="The Wrong Jedi" />

Some time later, Skywalker spoke to [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]] in the courtyard regarding the latter's belief that he was communing with the deceased Jedi Master [[Qui-Gon Jinn]]. Skywalker, who briefly heard Jinn's [[Force spirit|disembodied voice]] through the Force, expressed skepticism, but Yoda was convinced and began a journey to learn the secrets to retaining his consciousness after death.<ref name="Voices">{{TCW|Voices}}</ref> As part of this quest, he saw a vision of a peaceful [[Jedi Order]], one untouched by war. This vision placed him in the Jedi Temple training ground, where he saw many Jedi, including those who had been killed and had fallen to the [[dark side of the Force]], happily speaking to one another.<ref name="Destiny">{{TCW|Destiny (The Clone Wars)}}</ref> Upon his return to the Jedi Temple, Yoda spoke with fellow Jedi Council members [[Mace Windu]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] about his experiences, telling them that he was uncertain if it was possible for the Jedi Order to win the Clone Wars.<ref name="Sacrifice">{{TCW|Sacrifice (episode)}}</ref>

The end of the Clone Wars saw the destruction of the Jedi Order at the hands of the [[Sith]]. After declaring himself [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] and transforming the [[Galactic Republic]] into the [[Galactic Empire]],<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> the [[Sith Lord]] [[Darth Sidious]] transformed the Jedi Temple into the Imperial Palace.<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> He removed the ancient tree from the courtyard and, over two [[Standard decade|decades]] later, its two remaining fragments were located in an [[Imperial base (Vetine)|Imperial research lab]] on [[Vetine]]. They were [[Mission to Vetine|retrieved]] by [[Luke Skywalker]], the last known Jedi Knight and the son of Anakin Skywalker, and [[Lieutenant]] [[Shara Bey]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. Skywalker kept one of the fragments for himself and gifted the other to Bey, who planted it outside of her [[Wetyin's Colony|home]] on [[Yavin 4]].<ref name="Shattered Empire 4" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Ancient_Jedi_tree.png|thumb|right|250px|Concept art of the Jedi Temple training ground, by Andre Kirk]]
The training ground was first created for and seen in "[[The Wrong Jedi]]," an episode of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''.<ref name="The Wrong Jedi Trivia" /> Concept art for the training ground, including the ancient tree, was done by [[Andre Kirk]] in [[2011]].<ref name="The Wrong Jedi Concept Art">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-wrong-jedi-concept-art-gallery|text="The Wrong Jedi" Concept Art Gallery}}</ref>

